    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_325:0100094"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stage 6 is when the centre of the spot dries out, turns clear gray and is surrounded by a well-defined black ring, which is, in turn, surrounded by a bright yellow halo. These spots remain visible after the leaf has dried out because the ring persists.</rdfs:label>
