  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_325:0100095/3">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cropontology.org/rdf/CO_325:0100095"/>
    <ns1:altLabel xml:lang="en">3</ns1:altLabel>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Second-streak stage: the streaks may elongate slightly, but the most notable change is that in colour from reddish brown to dark brown or almost black, sometimes with a purplish tinge. The streak is now clearly visible on the upper surface of the leaf. The distribution of streaks at this stage of development varies in the same way as mentioned above. When streaks are very numerous, and more or less evenly distributed, the entire leaf blackens.</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
